  "totalCount": 929,
  "items": [
    {
      "bookId": "856239",
      "userVid": 205648472,
      "bookmarkId": "856239_19_3804-3822",
      "chapterUid": 19,
      "range": "3804-3822",
      "simplifiedRange": "",
      "traditionalRange": "",
      "markText": "不带评论的观察是人类智力的最高形式。",
      "totalCount": 82807
    },
    {
      "bookId": "856239",
      "userVid": 370196574,
      "bookmarkId": "856239_14_1116-1138",
      "chapterUid": 14,
      "range": "1116-1138",
      "simplifiedRange": "",
      "traditionalRange": "",
      "markText": "对他人的评价实际上反映了我们的需要和价值观。",
      "totalCount": 55332
    },
    {
      "bookId": "856239",
      "userVid": 83919912,
      "bookmarkId": "856239_3_817-912",
      "chapterUid": 3,
      "range": "817-912",
      "simplifiedRange": "",
      "traditionalRange": "",
      "markText": "言语上的指责、嘲讽、否定、说教以及任意打断、拒不回应、随意出口的评价和结论给我们带来的情感和精神上的创伤，甚至比肉体的伤害更加令人痛苦。这些无心或有意的语言暴力让人与人变得冷漠、隔膜、敌视。",
      "totalCount": 38970
    },
    {
      "bookId": "856239",
      "userVid": 250361029,
      "bookmarkId": "856239_33_710-768",
      "chapterUid": 33,
      "range": "710-768",
      "simplifiedRange": "",
      "traditionalRange": "",
      "markText": "如果我们通过批评来提出主张，人们的反应常常是申辩或反击。反之，如果我们直接说出需要，其他人就较有可能作出积极的回应。",
      "totalCount": 36839
    },
    {
      "bookId": "856239",
      "userVid": 265788721,
      "bookmarkId": "856239_6_1039-1065",
      "chapterUid": 6,
      "range": "1039-1065",
      "simplifiedRange": "",
      "traditionalRange": "",
      "markText": "非暴力生活的一个关键就是：感激生活的赐予，而不贪心。",
      "totalCount": 36195
    },
    {
      "bookId": "856239",
      "userVid": 388866292,
      "bookmarkId": "856239_8_963-1006",
      "chapterUid": 8,
      "range": "963-1006",
      "simplifiedRange": "",
      "traditionalRange": "",
      "markText": "也许我们并不认为自己的谈话方式是“暴力”的，但我们的语言确实常常引发自己和他人的痛苦。",
      "totalCount": 35744
    },
    {
      "bookId": "856239",
      "userVid": 388003985,
      "bookmarkId": "856239_16_3183-3200",
      "chapterUid": 16,
      "range": "3183-3200",
      "simplifiedRange": "",
      "traditionalRange": "",
      "markText": "我们无法强迫他人按我们的期待生活。",
      "totalCount": 34485
    },
    {
      "bookId": "856239",
      "userVid": 304960651,
      "bookmarkId": "856239_34_893-942",
      "chapterUid": 34,
      "range": "893-942",
      "simplifiedRange": "",
      "traditionalRange": "",
      "markText": "如果我们不看重自己的需要，别人可能也不会。实际上，如果直接说出需要，获得积极回应的可能性就会增加。",
      "totalCount": 31994
    },
    {
      "bookId": "856239",
      "userVid": 14837428,
      "bookmarkId": "856239_71_1823-1844",
      "chapterUid": 71,
      "range": "1823-1844",
      "simplifiedRange": "",
      "traditionalRange": "",
      "markText": "不论你选择做什么，了解自己为什么要那样做。",
      "totalCount": 28638
    },
    {
      "bookId": "856239",
      "userVid": 250504299,
      "bookmarkId": "856239_9_2644-2671",
      "chapterUid": 9,
      "range": "2644-2671",
      "simplifiedRange": "",
      "traditionalRange": "",
      "markText": "非暴力沟通的四个要素：1．观察2．感受3．需要4．请求",
      "totalCount": 24816
    },
    {
      "bookId": "856239",
      "userVid": 58082849,
      "bookmarkId": "856239_39_1882-1923",
      "chapterUid": 39,
      "range": "1882-1923",
      "simplifiedRange": "",
      "traditionalRange": "",
      "markText": "我们提出的请求越具体越好。如果我们的意思含糊不清，别人就难以了解我们到底想要什么。",
      "totalCount": 22372
    },
    {
      "bookId": "856239",
      "userVid": 304960651,
      "bookmarkId": "856239_16_3098-3123",
      "chapterUid": 16,
      "range": "3098-3123",
      "simplifiedRange": "",
      "traditionalRange": "",
      "markText": "一旦意识不到我们是自己的主人，我们就成了危险人物。",
      "totalCount": 21996
    },
    {
      "bookId": "856239",
      "userVid": 367915511,
      "bookmarkId": "856239_14_2042-2087",
      "chapterUid": 14,
      "range": "2042-2087",
      "simplifiedRange": "",
      "traditionalRange": "",
      "markText": "暴力的根源在于人们忽视彼此的感受与需要，而将冲突归咎于对方——至少大部分暴力的根源都是如此",
      "totalCount": 20628
    },
    {
      "bookId": "856239",
      "userVid": 351687197,
      "bookmarkId": "856239_5_1264-1330",
      "chapterUid": 5,
      "range": "1264-1330",
      "simplifiedRange": "",
      "traditionalRange": "",
      "markText": "我很希望这本书能帮助更多的人安静下来。使用暴力的人其实是因为他们内心的宁静遭到了破坏，所以他们才会用暴力的方式维护或寻求心灵的和平。",
      "totalCount": 20538
    },
    {
      "bookId": "856239",
      "userVid": 382982014,
      "bookmarkId": "856239_48_2903-2964",
      "chapterUid": 48,
      "range": "2903-2964",
      "simplifiedRange": "",
      "traditionalRange": "",
      "markText": "在非暴力沟通中，倾听他人意味着，放下已有的想法和判断，一心一意地体会他人。倾听的这种品质体现了它与理解以及同情之间的区别。",
      "totalCount": 17264
    },
    {
      "bookId": "856239",
      "userVid": 313704309,
      "bookmarkId": "856239_26_1867-1877",
      "chapterUid": 26,
      "range": "1867-1877",
      "simplifiedRange": "",
      "traditionalRange": "",
      "markText": "示弱有助于解决冲突。",
      "totalCount": 16599
    },
    {
      "bookId": "856239",
      "userVid": 19771693,
      "bookmarkId": "856239_35_1848-1889",
      "chapterUid": 35,
      "range": "1848-1889",
      "simplifiedRange": "",
      "traditionalRange": "",
      "markText": "真诚待人比委曲求全更为可贵。如果别人感到不安，我们可以认真地倾听，但无须责备自己。",
      "totalCount": 15708
    },
    {
      "bookId": "856239",
      "userVid": 388003985,
      "bookmarkId": "856239_22_546-641",
      "chapterUid": 22,
      "range": "546-641",
      "simplifiedRange": "",
      "traditionalRange": "",
      "markText": "非暴力沟通的第一个要素是观察。将观察和评论混为一谈，别人就会倾向于听到批评，并反驳我们。非暴力沟通是动态的语言，不主张绝对化的结论。它提倡在特定的时间和情境中进行观察，并清楚地描述观察结果。",
      "totalCount": 14960
    },
    {
      "bookId": "856239",
      "userVid": 20517169,
      "bookmarkId": "856239_16_2048-2069",
      "chapterUid": 16,
      "range": "2048-2069",
      "simplifiedRange": "",
      "traditionalRange": "",
      "markText": "我们可以用负责任的语言代替回避责任的语言。",
      "totalCount": 14265
    },
    {
      "bookId": "856239",
      "userVid": 19771693,
      "bookmarkId": "856239_32_2940-2978",
      "chapterUid": 32,
      "range": "2940-2978",
      "simplifiedRange": "",
      "traditionalRange": "",
      "markText": "我们可以通过“我（感到）……因为我……”这种表达方式来认识感受与自身的关系。",
      "totalCount": 13617
    }
  ],
